            <ArticleTitle>[Pathophysiology of vertebrogenic lumbar and leg pain (pain, sensory disorders, paralysis): review related to clinical aspects].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>131-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Vertebrogenic pain is attached to several types of spinal pathology: degenerative diseases of spinal structures, disc displacement with or without radicular disturbances, primary or metastatic tumors, inflammatory diseases. Present views on the pathogenetic mechanisms of the various types of vertebrogenic local radicular and pseudoradicular pain are discussed. Current opinions about pathogenesis of radicular deficit of sensibility and physical force are also presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
